WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Candied Natto</b>

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.860
Everybody burned...

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.410
My village was...

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.470
I...

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.450
...wasn't able to be like Lady Himiko.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:38.590
So you're all alone, too, huh?

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.980
That was how... you and 
I met for the first time.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:50.020
<b>September 5, 248</b>

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.570
Gun No. 10: Dogoo.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.750
I'd like you to help me again.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.180
In order to find more distinguished 
individuals who can fight against them,

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.390
I was thinking we'd head 
to the Frankish Kingdom.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.130
The Frankish Kingdom?

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.970
A country that came into being 
while you were asleep.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.910
How long was I asleep for?

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.060
I'd say about 300 years.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.760
I see...

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.950
Then the people and places 
I used to know are all long gone.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.340
Who is that?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.300
I found an interesting human.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.460
Thought he might make a good interlocutor 
for you, so I brought him back.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.320
I'm Saint-Germain.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.250
Nice to meet you, m'lady.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.040
What do you think you're doing?!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.500
It's a European greeting, 
but I see it wasn't to your liking.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:01.380
Now then, we've finished transforming the 
genes we collected so far into E-genes.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.350
Let's mix them into some human bloodlines.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.130
Leave it to us. 
We'll find the right people.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:14.280
A warrior's soul will be passed from parent 
to child with neither of them knowing.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.530
When the time comes, 
it will hatch and awaken.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.700
We have a few hundred years until 
they arrive on this planet.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.190
It's about how many warriors we can create, 
how many we can pass on by then.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.950
This is an important mission. 
Motivating, isn't it?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:41.980
Back then, I was convinced this man 
would be gone by the time I woke up again,

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:46.870
and that no one would remember me.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.990
Have you awakened?

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.420
What the...?!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.990
How long was I asleep this time?

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.660
Roughly 200 years, I guess.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.810
But you...?

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:11.710
That's just my constitution, m'lady.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.380
I told you, didn't I?

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:17.210
That he's an interesting human...

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:24.240
Now... shall we go look for 
new heroes together?

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:34.750
They had a mountain of daring warriors 
in that fortress. Why did you pick him?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:37.390
The only thing he's good for is his speed.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.670
Isn't that great? 
That's what I like about him!

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.610
The sleeping princess awakens.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.300
Where are we going?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.640
The country of your birth.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.440
Who for? What kind of person
 will you choose?

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.460
Of all people, him?

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.720
Isn't he the ruler of your homeland?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.710
Just like Himiko.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:18.290
He's nothing like her! 
He kills too many people!

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.290
But that's precisely why we 
need him in our fight.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.990
You mean you're going to entrust the planet's 
future to the soul of that blood-spattered guy?

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:32.060
Boy, it's been 1,200 years, but you 
haven't changed a bit, have you?

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.330
It's only been seven years for me!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.310
M'lady!

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.120
You didn't have to come after me.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.440
Don't say such lonesome things.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:00.090
I'm your interlocutor, aren't I?

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:05.780
From that point on, I began for the 
first time to live life like a human.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.620
A small hut,

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.490
laboring with the villagers,

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.160
the joy of the harvest,

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.950
the changing seasons.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.060
And then...

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.990
You're an eccentric one, aren't you?

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:26.400
You don't need to spend time 
with a grandma like me.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.640
What do you mean? You'll always 
be my adorable little lady.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:00.900
Not again...

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.190
I've lost my home again.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.910
You could start over?

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.450
No.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:15.730
After 1,500 years, I've finally learned...

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:22.440
...that there are some things in this 
world you must protect by any means.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.090
He must feel the same!

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.430
So you've returned to me.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.690
I will dedicate what little is left of 
my life to protecting this planet

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:35.670
and all life living on it.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.660
Good morning, Commander.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:46.810
"Commander"?

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.460
They've arrived?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:55.080
Yes. They'll reach the planet momentarily.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.390
So I've decided to entrust that 
organization to you.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.620
We've already disseminated the E-genes.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.840
Please wait. I'm not cut out for—

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.860
The burden on me is already too great.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.410
I'm just about at my limit.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.000
But...!

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.140
I'm sorry for the hand-me-up.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.400
Thank you, Iyo.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:28.110
Now it's up to you Earthlings.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.610
I'm counting on you.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.130
It seems like only yesterday...

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.500
And at last, here we are.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.580
Yes.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.810
But...

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.980
Gandhi to <i>Johnny Rico</i>. 
The battleship has withdrawn into the tunnel.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.630
<b>
 
 
 Atlantic side of the tunnel</b>

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.630
<b>
 
 
Dogoo High Speed Vessel 
<i>Johnny Rico</i> </b>

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.570
<i>Johnny Rico</i> to <i>Ellen Ripley</i>, 
prepare for underwater observation.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.050
<b>
 
 
Pacific side of the tunnel </b>

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.050
<b>
 
 
Dogoo High Speed Vessel 
<i>Ellen Ripley</i> </b>

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.030
If it follows the pattern it has been 
up till now, it'll come out in an hour.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.220
Gaudi here! Roger. I'm going in.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:23.360
Time for a break.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:30.880
As usual, it's just poking its head out 
every hour and then withdrawing.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.250
Honestly, we're lucky.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.230
We're no match for it at 
our current strength.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.470
It's true that we're low on troops.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:48.590
But there's no doubt that this is a 
do-or-die moment in the battle against them.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:57.660
Don't worry. This time, 
I'll protect my home at any cost.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:59.480
I'm counting on you.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:15.480
<b>Candied Natto
The commander's favorite </b>

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:18.170
<b>Nervous </b>

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:18.880
<b>Nervous </b>

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:19.670
<b>Nervous </b>

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:26.560
I knew this would happen, 
but still, just the two of us?!

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:29.380
You done jabbering?

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.520
I have something I need 
to talk to you about.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.850
Something he needs to 
talk to me about?!

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:40.840
Our eyes met! Ahh!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:38.960
<b>Grab</b>

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:39.760
<b>Grab</b>

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:40.510
<b>Grab</b>

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.100
Huh?

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.550
<b>Empty </b>

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:44.900
None left!

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.050
Hey, are you...

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:52.360
W-W-W-W-W-W-W-W-W—

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.280
W-What? What? What?

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.230
What were you doing over there?

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:56.730
Huh?

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:01.510
You were in front of the 
<i>Clayton Forrester </i>at that moment.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:06.890
That must mean you knew the squid 
was aiming for the mothership—

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:12.870
from before you could see its body, considering 
how long it would take to get back there.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:14.820
How did you know?

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:19.100
How? Uh...

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:22.400
I guess I just happened... 
to have that feeling?

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.260
Did your E-gene tell you?

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.440
Huh?

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:32.670
Well, I dunno about that... 
something like intuition?

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.060
Why didn't you tell anyone, 
if you knew?

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.240
Huh?

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.840
Did you want to take care of it 
yourself and be a hero?

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:41.810
L-Like I'd—

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.940
...do that? Of course you wouldn't.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:47.690
I'm always watchin' ya, 
so I know what you're like.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:52.800
What! Watching me? 
Always? Know what?!

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.080
<b>Surprisingly overly self-conscious</b>

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:53.910
<b>Misunderstanding</b>

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:56.170
But I barely have any battle experience!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:13:00.400
That the predication came true was just by 
chance... it just popped into my head...

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.580
I dunno why...

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.220
I don't want to die yet.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.040
Huh?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.770
They decided to go ahead with 
the operation to capture the tunnel.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:13.560
The only ones being sent in are 
the First and Second Platoons.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:15.540
Only us?

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:19.800
Right now, the commander and 
Vidocq are strategizing.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.050
But there's something bothering me.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.020
Something about this is dangerous.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:31.360
My E-gene is saying it needs you.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.900
N-Needs?

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:35.500
Yeah. The things that pop into your head.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:37.770
But...

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:45.420
The legendary killer who sensed the London 
police closing in on him and got away...

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:48.400
...says he needs you.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.230
Still not convinced?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.550
Asai, you were a traitor?!

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:20.690
Lord Nobunaga! At this rate, we'll be 
flanked by them and the Asakura!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:30.380
Lord Nobunaga! I will bring up the rear!

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.350
Make your retreat while I distract them!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:33.460
Saru!

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:41.520
And the one protecting their eggs, 
their original cells, is the battleship.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.630
Now projecting the updated 
X-ray map of the tunnel!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:53.770
Can't we get a more accurate 
reading of its tentacle strength?

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:55.280
There's not enough data!

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:57.690
If we approach from this angle...

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.320
I have something to say!

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:08.000
I received no report of your return. 
What's going on, Nobunagun?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.600
Uh... err...

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:13.260
...about the plan to capture the tunnel...

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:17.100
Um... I guess I have an opinion? Or...

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:17.950
Hey...

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:22.390
Think before you open your mouth.

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:27.490
This isn't the kind of place an amateur can 
ramble off whatever pops into their head.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:32.970
The operation to capture the tunnel 
is our most important yet.

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:37.850
Our approach to the Invasion Objects will largely 
depend on whether we win or lose here.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:43.570
You could say this battle decides how 
well we can minimize human casualties.

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:47.060
Do you understand?! 
People's lives are at stake!

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.240
That's...

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.000
That's why I came!

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:01.120
Let's hear her out.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:09.880
You're thinking to take out the battleship 
and enter the tunnel

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:13.200
because that's where the enemies carrying 
the original cells are holed up, right?

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:20.480
But at present, the battleship is just popping 
in and out of the entrance of the tunnel.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:24.250
If it wants to intercept us, 
that's a pretty weird way to do it.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.400
Yeah, it's like he's provoking us. 
Pisses me off!

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.490
That's the point!

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:28.870
Huh?

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:33.300
Since it's doing that, we're focused 
entirely on the entrance to the tunnel!

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:40.640
While we're busy there, the main force is 
probably digging new tunnels to escape.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:45.240
The battleship is a rear guard 
buying evacuation time!

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.530
That's what I think.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.280
Vidocq.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.290
Y-Yes?

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:56.890
R-Right. That scenario is conceivable.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:01.410
Or rather, it's probably... correct.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:04.360
Shit, why didn't I think of that?

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:08.120
Can we deduce where they're 
attempting to escape to?

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:09.550
Well...

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:16.610
...they know we're on our guard along the coast 
near the tunnel and the Panama Canal.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.990
Lake Nicaragua. Perhaps they 
mean to take refuge here.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:33.720
If they leave the tunnel and disperse in open water, 
we'll have a hell of a time finding them.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:37.040
We've got to catch up with them 
before that happens.

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:40.880
All the more reason to find a way to 
break the battleship's guard—

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:42.510
We don't need to do that.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.430
What?!

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:49.860
U-Uh... it's just... instead of attacking from 
the rear, where the battleship is,

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.880
let's attack from the front, 
where they don't expect us.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:53.580
Hey!

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.460
You have a plan, huh?

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.540
Y-Yeah!

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:06.890
Of course, we can't get around in 
front them while they are tunneling.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.130
So...

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:14.470
We'll get them to change their 
path and come out on land...

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:21.080
...where we'll be waiting to
 intercept and annihilate them!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:25.050
Of all the stupid—! You really think 
it'll be so easy to lure them out?!

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.060
We can!

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:26.570
Wha—!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:32.240
And to do it, we've got to use 
everything we've got.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.750
<b>Lake Nicaragua</b>

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:38.300
I'm an old man declared unfit for battle. 
What're they draggin' me out for?

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.800
Is this revenge for training 
Nobunagun so roughly?

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:42.540
Whaddya think, Newton?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.070
Why do I have to do 
such a stupid job?

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.830
I'm gonna trample her when 
we're done with this.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:51.600
What?! You're crazy!

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:53.030
No...

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:58.730
If we combine the power of Capa and Newton,
the calculations do say it should be possible.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:01.690
So where should we have them come out?

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:08.520
Estimating their route and speed 
based on geological data,

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:12.360
and taking into consideration the 
effect those two's powers will have...

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:15.130
Got it.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.540
This is our main battleground.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:25.390
<b>The Republic of Costa Rica 
Upala</b>

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:25.390
The evacuation of all inhabitants 
has been confirmed.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.730
Attack squad, prepare for battle.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:28.860
Roger.

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:32.860
What a splendid plan! 
I just wonder if we can pull it off.

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:34.780
I know you'll do great, Geronimo!

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:36.570
You're one to pep talk, Gaudi.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:37.110
Hm?

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.270
You've got a lot of responsibility here.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:41.190
Yeah...

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.050
Man, for me to get roped into fighting...

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.660
I'm in the special task force, 
for cryin' out loud.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.440
We're running short, Hunter.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:55.480
Well, a sulky blade is better than none.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.250
Do your best! We're too short-handed 
to gather your remains if you die.

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.970
<b>California, U.S.A. 
San Diego Naval Base</b>

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.130
This is worse than the 
traffic jams in L.A.

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:09.760
Wonder what's gonna go down.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:15.170
It's hard to believe there's something out 
on the water that we need to unleash these on.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:17.810
<b>3 km southeast of Upala</b>

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:21.100
All right, nice and easy, okay?

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:22.260
I don't like this.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:26.280
The princess is supposed to be the 
only one allowed to ride me!

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:31.270
The new recruit from your 
platoon came up with this plan?

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.560
Yeah. Honestly, I was surprised, too.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:35.950
Ah... but...

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:36.320
Hm?

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:41.820
I guess she's been surprising me ever 
since we first met in Taiwan.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.300
More importantly, when we're done here,
 can I run her over?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.290
N-No, thaaat's not okay...

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.360
The battleship class is the problem!

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:52.980
If another one showed up as 
reinforcement, we'd be in trouble.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.100
Lure it out!

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:57.900
Hold it at the tunnel's entrance!

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.420
This'll never work!

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.550
We don't have enough E-gene 
holders to bring in more!

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:04.090
One is enough!

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:10.390
There will be a single E-gene holder 
fighting the battleship.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.860
I'll do it!

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:50.940
Here we go!

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:28.860
Hey, where does the name for the 
Stone Forest operation come from?

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:30.800
Th-That's top secret!

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:33.890
"Stone Forest" in Japanese 
would be "Ishi no—"

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:38.270
Next time, Gun No. 11: 
Operation Stone Forest, Part 1.

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:39.680
So that's what it means...
